{"availability":"available","full":"AHD184/image-deepfake-detection","name":"image-deepfake-detection","description":"Face-based deepfake image detection system using PyTorch, ResNet18, and Gradio, deployed on Hugging Face Spaces.","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2026-03-06T14:20:01Z","updated":"2026-05-27T13:29:01Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/AHD184/Image_Deepfake_Detection_System","topics":["computer-vision","deepfake-detection","gradio","huggingface-spaces","image-classification","machine-learning-models","pytorch","resnet18"],"demo":"https://huggingface.co/spaces/AHD184/Image_Deepfake_Detection_System","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:09.572Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:09.572Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T22:34:09.572Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T22:34:09.572Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["A face-based image deepfake detection project built with PyTorch, ResNet18, and Gradio.","This project is an end-to-end deepfake image detection system that classifies uploaded face images as Fake, Real, or Uncertain. It uses a ResNet18-based transfer learning model trained on real and fake face datasets, and the final model is deployed through a public Gradio web app on Hugging Face Spaces.","The main goal of this project was to build a complete machine learning pipeline rather than only train a model. The project includes dataset preparation, preprocessing, training, evaluation, single-image inference, and public deployment."],"features":["Image upload interface using Gradio","Fake / Real / Uncertain prediction","Class probability display","ResNet18 transfer learning model","PyTorch training and evaluation pipeline"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/AHD184/image-deepfake-detection/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"65a082f70c237188bc6eb92a6a277e64c71657ec44db4337bc254cd9932a9ab9","ext